  "description": "This is a retrospective full planning application for the retention of an existing single-storey ancillary outbuilding within the rear residential garden of the property.\n\nThe application is submitted because, whilst the development is otherwise consistent with the principles of domestic outbuildings ordinarily permitted under Class E of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015, the structure is located within 2 metres of the site boundary and has an overall built height of approximately 2.74 metres, exceeding the permitted development height threshold of 2.50 metres by approximately 0.24 metres.\n\nThe purpose of this application is therefore solely to regularise this modest height exceedance.\n\nOutbuilding was constructed but replacement of rear outbuilding fails to meet the permitted development criteria. The outbuilding is within 2m of the boundary and exceeds 2.5m in height.\n\nTherefore, this application is retrospective planning application, as advised by Planning Enforcement officer. \n\nThe height of the outbuilding is currently 2.74m and plan dimensions are 6.02m long x 3.52m wide.\n\nClient therefore requests an approval of the current height which is about 2.74m, which is 0.24m higher than the allowable 2.5m.",
